/-!
# Weight-one form on Γ₁(M) with v vartheta j = w²

Theorem statement: `ModularForm.exists_gamma1_weightOne_ne_zero_and_mul_thetaL_eq_qExpansion_sq`
(`ad2d7347-49c0-57ec-b6d2-4ab3b26be5d6`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `a139a896-0051-5778-b2a2-ec10695bd075`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $M$ be a natural number with $5 \le M$ (and $M \neq 0$). The assertion is the existence of a
modular form $w$ of weight $1$ for the group $\Gamma_1(M)$, regarded as a subgroup of
$\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$, together with a Laurent series $v \in \mathbb{C}((q))$, such that three
conditions hold. First, $w \neq 0$. Second, $v$ lies in [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange ℂ
(ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma1 M))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is,
in the intermediate field of $\mathbb{C}((q))$ over $\mathbb{C}$ generated by the coefficientwise
images under $\mathbb{Q} \to \mathbb{C}$ of the elements of `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma1 M)`, the
subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by all quotients
$\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_f / \mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_g$ in which $f$ and $g$
are modular forms of some common weight $k$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$, $p_f$ and $p_g$ are integral power
series satisfying the predicate `IsIntegralQExp` with respect to $f$ and $g$, and
$\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_g \neq 0$. Third, $v \cdot \vartheta j =
\bigl(\text{$q$-expansion of } w\bigr)^2$ in $\mathbb{C}((q))$, where $\vartheta j$ is `thetaL ℂ
(jqModC ℂ)`, the operator $f \mapsto q\,\mathrm{d}f/\mathrm{d}q$ applied to $q^{-1}\cdot(E_4^3 \cdot
\mathrm{dedekindEtaUnitInv})$ with coefficients pushed to $\mathbb{C}$, and the square is that of
the image of `UpperHalfPlane.qExpansion 1 w` in $\mathbb{C}((q))$.

This supplies the odd-weight analogue of the multiplier $(\vartheta j)^m$: a square root of a
suitable power of $\vartheta j$ up to a function on $X_1(M)$, realised by a non-zero weight-one form
such as an Eisenstein series attached to an odd Dirichlet character. It is used by
[`ModularForm.exists_linearIndependent_gamma1_dimFormula_le_card_of_odd`]
(thm.html#ModularForm.exists_linearIndependent_gamma1_dimFormula_le_card_of_odd)
in the proof of the upper bound for the dimension of spaces of modular forms of odd weight on
$\Gamma_1(M)$.

